      "guid": "com.maschine.notificationfilter",
      "name": "NotificationFilter",
      "slug": "notificationfilter",
      "teaser": "Gives you full control over the notification popups that appear during raids.",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/lDKM4wTNULJR7fMAPSfQkYDOMPEMXzqFtNiqOFIz.png",
      "downloads": 607,
      "favourites_count": 7,
      "description": "<p>You’re all surely familiar with those annoying tasks that practically always fail unless you make a concerted effort to complete them (like “Friend Among Strangers,” “Small Business – Part 2,” etc.). <br />\nThe constant failure notifications eventually got on my nerves so much that I created this little mod to silence the pop-ups without having to lower the overall UI volume.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Silence notification sounds</strong> - Mutes the sounds for task and subtask completions, XP gain, and skill level-ups during raids. Notifications still appear visually so you don’t miss anything.</li>\n<li><strong>Hide XP notifications</strong> - Removes the XP gain popups (looting, healing, etc.) that clutter the screen during a raid.</li>\n<li><strong>Hide skill level-up notifications</strong> - Optionally hides the popup when a skill reaches a new level.</li>\n<li><strong>Hide skill progress notifications</strong> - Optionally hides the “Skill X increased by Y” popup that appears on every XP gain.</li>\n<li><strong>Notification duration</strong> - Extend how long popups stay on screen: normal, 2× longer, or infinite (click to dismiss).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All options are configurable via the <strong>F12 menu</strong> (BepInEx ConfigurationManager).</p>\n<h2>Notes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Sound suppression and notification hiding only applies during active raids. Hideout and main menu are unaffected.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>As usual, unzip into your SPT folder.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Let me know if you run into any problems or have suggestions for improvement.</p>\n",
